    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen004.png",
    "sha256": "b4bc3e7bcd686caef77516dc2b808cb5f9be5a9c85811671b1d3e860429ec240",
    "k": 3,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This shows that racial diversity is not occurring everywhere.",
    "zh": "这表明，种族多样化并没有发生在每个地方。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "occur"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen005.png",
    "sha256": "085fad6194bbda387af15d0d98f3f4d8d63a00af3f9ee1547667097e60bb5bb8",
    "k": 4,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Then what about other types of diversity?",
    "zh": "那么，其他类型的多样性呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "what about"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen006.png",
    "sha256": "cc57324cbe4b3a4dec34595530926b30ce0b17aac077ff29dafc9da083db8b72",
    "k": 5,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Right. The second type of diversity is age diversity.",
    "zh": "对。第二种多样性是年龄多样性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "age diversity"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen007.png",
    "sha256": "bbc7c9478e62ba741a576ed12522cb0492f85bb355edbaf0cab4400c269eae90",
    "k": 6,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And there are some interesting age gaps developing between states.",
    "zh": "各州之间正在形成一些值得关注的年龄差距。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "age gap"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen008.png",
    "sha256": "1c9d4b509a0b38c770f135a06081bdfdcb05dd1e2ed206de8e0443a2ccb6fd64",
    "k": 7,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For example, there is a large gap between the average age of the 5 states with the youngest populations and the 5 states with the oldest populations.",
    "zh": "例如，人口最年轻的五个州与人口最年长的五个州之间，平均年龄相差很大。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "average age"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen009.png",
    "sha256": "3399997f87d04cc3f306db2d50be8785fab4c749bf5015cda06129202530862a",
    "k": 8,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This, of course, is well-known.",
    "zh": "当然，这一点众所周知。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "well-known"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen010.png",
    "sha256": "d49d1a75395b91f6b85c2d94479f27a1d8c1839c2c57f1b8ade4a7998315b262",
    "k": 9,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What is less discussed is the difference between the racial makeup of younger and older populations.",
    "zh": "较少有人讨论的是，年轻人口与年长人口在种族构成上的差异。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "racial makeup"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen011.png",
    "sha256": "770b3eec8b3184bab78294ebc66de53fdff675e50ea7bf512d741ca9d19aacb8",
    "k": 10,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Most of the populations having the greatest racial diversity are younger on average than the populations with greater Caucasian representation.",
    "zh": "种族构成最多样化的人口群体，其平均年龄大多低于高加索裔占比较高的人口群体。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "representation"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen012.png",
    "sha256": "5ae349161fb493fe4eed5513fcf37163b5ca283a3ca3183157c5c6763239adae",
    "k": 11,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It is also well-known that Caucasians tend to be more affluent than other ethnic groups on average.",
    "zh": "另一个众所周知的事实是，高加索裔的平均富裕程度往往高于其他族裔。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "affluent"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen013.png",
    "sha256": "cab90ea15c06606da76b65ca20ab73e5be3b3cf4f3a0b81a0ad656bc6fe72359",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In our pay-as-you-go social security system, workers are taxed to pay the benefit of retirees.",
    "zh": "在我们的现收现付社会保障制度中，在职人员缴纳的税款用于支付退休人员的福利。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pay-as-you-go"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "72206fee0e45ed34aab9dff2f36cbc720627159e14dd6843eae1aac66ed9af6a",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So this could lead to a future where wealth is systematically redistributed from younger, poorer minorities ",
    "zh": "因此，今后可能会出现这样的局面：财富通过制度性的再分配，从较年轻、较贫穷的少数族裔群体，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "redistribute"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "e7df5d69d959d637e7c379c32bc3593b6f987a6b187cc0ee9b5f79032a49beaa",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "to older, wealthier whites.",
    "zh": "流向较年长、较富裕的白人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "wealthy"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "e9dcb4eed5548c3e5233c8437a09791aa8e094133d0c49f51dd319093de8ddbb",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This is a very interesting point.",
    "zh": "这是一个很值得关注的观点。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "point"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "9cfca6b8bb4ee93c0f02bb3ad7ece08c19c4720880124bc4541a4314b59d27b1",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Then what is the third type of diversity in the US?",
    "zh": "那么，美国的第三种多样性是什么？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "type"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "d5f8b644361d0136ecb784632c796da2d496f55848d4cb0a7b13e8b2350deee5",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The third is religious diversity.",
    "zh": "第三种是宗教多样性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "religious diversity"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "e52d6eeb0b198dc76ea3b5788158d1756afea3b6f41057bcf4117983e7c94ef1",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Immigration from India, Pakistan, and the Middle East brought radically increased numbers of Hindus and Muslims to the US.",
    "zh": "来自印度、巴基斯坦和中东的移民，使美国的印度教徒和穆斯林人数大幅增加。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "radically"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "d4be509c2dd0e46902293a7579ee170b1f1506a8c9d8e145edfc959d2117f756",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And Chinese, Vietnamese, Japanese and other Asian immigrants increased the numbers of Buddhists.",
    "zh": "而中国、越南、日本以及其他亚洲国家的移民，使佛教徒人数增加了。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "immigrant"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "1ba5fa6825f68b59042ab3c617629d8c396d54e6f913dabf3d690da77e880544",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Oh, I see.",
    "zh": "哦，我明白了。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "I see"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "e14a264b62805ac28e72139dbab01acb796553f1e296b089980f63564af277b3",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But the point is that these religions didn’t settle everywhere.",
    "zh": "但关键在于，这些宗教并没有在所有地方落地生根。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "settle"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "6b2cd1a20a1ab5868833d49313d034608dd49520893d5705805a67630b59039d",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They settled mainly in California, and major northeastern and mid-western cities, such as New York, Philadelphia, Chicago and Minneapolis.",
    "zh": "它们主要扎根于加州，以及美国东北部和中西部的大城市，例如纽约、费城、芝加哥和明尼阿波利斯。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mainly"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "af2ee6f084fbfb315561eeaa63f1d11111cfcda8e0d79fb8e02efb8da6e54293",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "From 1990 to 2000, the number of Muslims in New York city grew from 600,000 to nearly 1 million.",
    "zh": "从1990年到2000年，纽约市的穆斯林人数从60万增至近100万。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "grow from"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "c486e1285bc03171dfe6723358410f1f4264c4543beaa6959df5a50fae657504",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In the Los Angeles area, there are now more than 300 Buddhist temples.",
    "zh": "在洛杉矶地区，如今已有三百多座佛教寺庙。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Buddhist temple"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "082e1d70567fd1ebb931910e5fd735b15748ac77c4323aafdde771900b947dae",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So we see that many parts of the US are truly becoming more diverse ",
    "zh": "所以我们可以看到，美国的许多地方确实正在变得更多元；",
    "vocabulary": [
      "diverse"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "fefb742ea6ec6b11c4b8c38a29945ec62816cb04b464e4ea902ee41045502326",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "while at the same time others are essentially remaining the same in terms of race, age and religion.",
    "zh": "与此同时，另一些地方在种族、年龄和宗教方面基本保持不变。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "essentially",
      "religion"
    ]
  },
